  "title": "A Claude worker or reviewer round shows each step while it runs, as a Codex round does, and keeps its final result exactly as today",
  "public_title": "Show live progress for Claude rounds",
  "scope": [
    "bin/adapters/**",
    "bin/fm-herdr.py",
    "bin/lib/**",
    "design/design.md",
    "tests/**",
    "design/tasks/T-287.json"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "Why. A Claude worker or reviewer round prints nothing until it ends: the run log and the `fm follow` view show only a growing silence counter, so a round that works for an hour looks the same as one that hangs. Codex rounds already show their steps.",
    "What, live steps. While a Claude round runs, each step appears as it happens in the run log and in the `fm follow` view: which file it reads or edits, which command it runs, and a short line of its own text. This uses the Claude CLI's own streaming output.",
    "What, final result unchanged. A Claude round that completes keeps the same final answer, verdict, model record, turn count, signing and handoff as today.",
    "What, incomplete stream. For rounds launched with streaming output, a stream that ends without a result event, or that holds a malformed event line anywhere (a line starting with `{` that does not parse as JSON), even when a valid result event follows, makes the round incomplete: no final answer is recorded and it is never reported as a completed round.",
    "What, other lines. Lines that do not start with `{`, such as connection-retry notices and `fm-sandbox:` lines, are skipped as they are today, and the last result event in the stream is the one that counts.",
    "What, silence. For a Claude round, the vendor-silence time that the `fm follow` view shows, and its \"possibly stuck\" mark, are measured from its latest step.",
    "What, old records. Stored transcripts of past Claude rounds in the old single-JSON output format stay readable without conversion, and rounds already running with the old output format finish under the previous rules.",
    "Docs, design. `design/design.md` §11 (Self-update), in its \"Owners and wakes\" subsection, describes Claude rounds as streaming their steps instead of buffering until the end.",
    "Docs, adapter contract. `bin/adapters/_contract.md` names Claude's streaming output flag where it now names `--output-format json`, and says the model is read from the stream's final result event.",
    "Done, tests. A stub that reads the output flag it is given (the old single JSON object for `--output-format json`, and the Claude CLI's real streaming event shapes, with delays between them, for the streaming flag) proves: steps appear in the run log before the round ends (`claude stream: steps appear while running`); the final answer, verdict and model record equal those of the same round in the old output format (`claude stream: final result unchanged`); a cut-off stream, and a stream with a malformed event line before a valid result, are reported incomplete (`claude stream: cut-off stream is incomplete`, `claude stream: malformed line is incomplete`); silence counts from the last step (`claude stream: silence from last step`). `steps appear while running` and `malformed line is incomplete` fail on the base; `final result unchanged`, `cut-off stream is incomplete` and `silence from last step` are regression checks.",
    "Done, existing tests. Existing tests that assert `--output-format json` for Claude are updated to the streaming flag.",
    "Out of scope. The Codex adapter; how rounds are launched or sandboxed; the board layout."
  ],
